{"id": "EUVD-2026-12810", "enisaUuid": "02f69530-b8c3-3cea-8eb2-79b7440262f6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntcp: secure_seq: add back ports to TS offset\n\nThis reverts 28ee1b746f49 (\"secure_seq: downgrade to per-host timestamp offsets\")\n\ntcp_tw_recycle went away in 2017.\n\nZhouyan Deng reported off-path TCP source port leakage via\nSYN cookie side-channel that can be fixed in multiple ways.\n\nOne of them is to bring back TCP ports in TS offset randomization.\n\nAs a bonus, we perform a single siphash() computation\nto provide both an ISN and a TS offset.", "datePublished": "2026-03-18T10:05:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:39:02", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e873e8c16b2fb743a381a9e59c108e63512301ec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5da5662181ef8a251e3ba564903002c2e87de452", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eae2f14ab2efccdb7480fae7d42c4b0116ef8805", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/46e5b0d7cf55821527adea471ffe52a5afbd9caf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/165573e41f2f66ef98940cf65f838b2cb575d9d1"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4hcm-qg7j-cc3v", "CVE-2026-23247"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a358544-168b-3304-bcef-d54441913efe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "28ee1b746f493b7c62347d714f58fbf4f70df4f0 <5da5662181ef8a251e3ba564903002c2e87de452"}, {"id": "23bdeaba-5a37-337e-b7b7-ae82814c6f88", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}, {"id": "23c36a3c-fe0b-3873-a1fa-50852b4319d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.11"}, {"id": "3d889d0e-1acd-3535-a117-99720b0144d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "443fac9f2618b93cbc5ab068dc594530236b3a23"}, {"id": "5a7ae8e7-e274-3016-a5d7-029fa1e1722a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_v